**Problem 3:**

Create a function file `aboda_final_p3.m`:

```matlab
function [mu, var] = aboda_final_p3(eigFunc, m, tol, N)
    iterations = zeros(N, 1);
    rng(0); % Set random seed to 0
    for i = 1:N
        A = rand(m);
        A = 0.5 * (A + A'); % Make the matrix symmetric
        [~, ~, iter] = eigFunc(A, tol);
        iterations(i) = iter;
    end
    mu = mean(iterations);
    var = var(iterations);
end
```

You can now use these functions to calculate the spectrum of a matrix and analyze the performance of the "Pure" QR Algorithm and the QR Algorithm with Wilkinson shift. Additionally, you can compute the mean and variance of the number of iterations required to solve the problem.

Please replace "aboda" with a suitable name that corresponds to your requirement.

